    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 4e22c8dbe915bfa9131486395c4237898532370d -->\nReview at head 4e22c8dbe. Read, not built: the PR is from a fork, so its code does not run on the maintainer's runners, and no local build slot was free.\n\nThe change reads well:\n- `chamfer_open_runs` validates the parameters first, refuses an empty selection, a non-finite corner depth, a chain with no model wall at the programmed depth, and a collapsed segment. Each refusal says what to do. The material side comes from a model read at the two chamfer heights, so climb does not depend on the stored edge direction. Provenance is in the file header.\n- The selection wiring adds `Chamfer2D` beside Contour and PlasmaProfile for open runs (#670 pattern). No new command, so no MCP tool is owed.\n- The pinning tests cover one edge, connected edges as one run, separate chains as separate passes, and no credit for an unselected edge. File sizes obey the 400-line rule. `docs/decisions/2988-chamfer-open-edge-chains.md` is in the PR. No snapshot PNG is touched.\n- The red heavy step you report is not yours: on a platform outside the three pins, `bore_path_matches` still uses the pre-solidcore fallback band, so the same step is red on plain main. I filed #3085 for it.\n\nOne requested change:\n- The three new refusal branches have no pinning test. Add a test for each: a run with a collapsed segment, an open edge with no model wall at the chamfer depth, and picks that are open runs under Boundary settings that shape an area. Assert the refusal and the message name. This is safety-floor code, so each refusal needs its proof.\n\nLabels are not changed by this review.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
